<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.size(); (\result.get(i) <=> (bb.get(i / 8) & (1 << (i % 8))) != 0);</code>

Explanation:
- `\result != null` ensures that the returned BitSet is not null.
- `\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.size();` iterates over each bit in the resulting BitSet.
- `(\result.get(i) <=> (bb.get(i / 8) & (1 << (i % 8))) != 0)` checks that each bit in the resulting BitSet matches the corresponding bit in the ByteBuffer `bb`. The expression `(bb.get(i / 8) & (1 << (i % 8))) != 0` extracts the i-th bit from the ByteBuffer.
--------------------
<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.size(); (\result.get(i) <=> (bb.get(i / 8) & (1L << (i % 8))) != 0);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result != null && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \result.size(); (\result.get(i) == ((bb.get(i / 8) & (1 << (i % 8))) != 0));</code>
--------------------
